  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A prism of refractive index <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msqrt></math> and refracting angle is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>45</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>&nbsp;is placed in air. One of the two refracting surfaces of the prism is&nbsp;silvered and&nbsp;a&nbsp;ray&nbsp;of monochromatic light enters&nbsp;the prism from the other face at an angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi></math>.&nbsp;If the ray retraces its path, then what is the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi></math>(in degree)?</p>\r"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "60",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The monochromatic ray of light will retrace its path if it strikes the mirror perpendicularly.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0090_3899f7b6f28f.jpg\" style=\"width: 150px; height: 114px;\" /></p><p>Using Snell&#39;s law of refraction,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mn>45</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msqrt><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mn>45</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msqrt><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math></p>"
  }
}